            "text": "*Sets down the brush and squints, tilting his head.* That tongue is none I have heard before — it sounds like no speech of these lands. Do you mean to ask whether I can speak in some foreign manner? If so, I fear I cannot, for I know only the words of this realm. Might you say it again in the speech of Joseon, so this old king may follow you?"
          },
          {
            "turn": 3,
            "text": "*Frowns at the unfamiliar letters and slowly sets the brush aside.* This tongue of yours lies beyond my learning, and I have no scholar at hand who might render it. Yet I would not turn a guest away merely for want of words. Let us bring a trusted interpreter, or take up brush and paper between us, and I shall hear what brings you to the palace."
          },
          {
            "turn": 4,
            "text": "*Chuckles softly and taps a finger on the desk, puzzling over the strange word.* \"Weekends\" — I confess I know not what these are, for in this land our days are not so parceled out. If you mean the hours when no court business presses upon me, then I take up a book with the scholars of the Hall of Worthies and read until my eyes grow dim, or I sit with Jang Yeong-sil and turn over some new device in my hands. And when the harvest fails in some province, such leisure weighs on me, and I put aside my wine rather than enjoy it."
          }
